{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TNQj5pYGJoisa1urB2ajnz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"seismic shear strain depth profile closed-form 1D site response gamma partial derivative displacement depth\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Site-Specific Dynamic Ground Response Analysis - March 2022\",\"url\":\"https://dot.ca.gov/-/media/dot-media/programs/engineering/documents/geotechnical-services/202203-gm-sitespecificdgra-a11y.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Guidelines for Estimation of Shear Wave Velocity Profiles\",\"url\":\"https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/webpeer-2012-08-bernard_r._wair_jason_t._dejong_and_thomas_shantz.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Review of Parameters and Methods for Seismic Site Response\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3263/15/4/128\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of 1-D Non-linear Site Response Analysis using ...\",\"url\":\"https://secure.tcc.co.nz/ei/images/ICEGE15%20Papers/Hashash%20269.00.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of 1-D seismic site response modeling of sand using centrifuge experiments - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726115001761\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 12 GEOTECHNICAL SEISMIC ANALYSIS GEOTECHNICAL DESIGN MANUAL\",\"url\":\"https://www.scdot.org/content/dam/scdot-legacy/business/pdf/geotech/2022-by-chapter/Chapter12-GeotechnicalSeismicAnalysis-01112022.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Applicability of 1D site response analysis to shallow sedimentary basins: A critical evaluation through physics‐based 3D ground motion simulations - Huang - 2024 - Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/eqe.4142\"},{\"title\":\"NC92Soil: A computer code for deterministic and stochastic 1D equivalent linear seismic site response analyses | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374947177_NC92Soil_A_computer_code_for_deterministic_and_stochastic_1D_equivalent_linear_seismic_site_response_analyses\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An innovative computer code for 1D seismic response analysis including shear strength of soils\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/284755269_An_innovative_computer_code_for_1D_seismic_response_analysis_including_shear_strength_of_soils\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of One-Dimensional Seismic Site Response Analyses at Small to Large Strain Levels\",\"url\":\"https://digital.lib.washington.edu/researchworks/handle/1773/37067\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on seismic shear strain depth profiles in 1D site response analysis. The results provide comprehensive information about seismic site response analysis methods.\n\nThe search returned several relevant resources covering 1D seismic site response analysis, including discussions of:\n\n1. **Site Response Analysis Methods**: The analysis techniques can be categorized as linear (L), equivalent linear (EL), and nonlinear (NL) analyses in one dimension (1D), two dimensions (2D) and three dimensions (3D), with 1D analyses relying on the assumption that all soil layers are horizontal and infinite, and dynamic response considers vertical propagation of horizontal shear waves.\n\n2. **Shear Strain Profiles**: Studies compute lateral displacements, accelerations, shear strains, spectral accelerations, and Arias Intensities, with particular focus on understanding shear strain distributions with depth.\n\n3. **Depth Variation Effects**: In the equivalent linear (EL) analysis method, the equation of motion for the vertically propagating seismic shear waves is solved in the frequency domain.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about closed-form solutions for shear strain depth profiles, the mathematical derivations involving partial derivatives of displacement with respect to depth, or explicit formulations using gamma (γ) notation as partial derivatives. If you need more specific technical information about these mathematical relationships, you may want to search for academic papers or textbooks focused on wave propagation theory in geotechnical engineering.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"a3fee75d-c907-455f-83ff-d3cc12994907","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:47:46.841Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"seismic shear strain depth profile closed-form 1D site response gamma partial derivative displacement depth","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018UQehyYu9csgTBdAMfs7nn","content":[{"title":"Site-Specific Dynamic Ground Response Analysis - March 2022","url":"https://dot.ca.gov/-/media/dot-media/programs/engineering/documents/geotechnical-services/202203-gm-sitespecificdgra-a11y.pdf"},{"title":"Guidelines for Estimation of Shear Wave Velocity Profiles","url":"https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/webpeer-2012-08-bernard_r._wair_jason_t._dejong_and_thomas_shantz.pdf"},{"title":"A Review of Parameters and Methods for Seismic Site Response","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3263/15/4/128"},{"title":"Evaluation of 1-D Non-linear Site Response Analysis using ...","url":"https://secure.tcc.co.nz/ei/images/ICEGE15%20Papers/Hashash%20269.00.pdf"},{"title":"Evaluation of 1-D seismic site response modeling of sand using centrifuge experiments - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726115001761"},{"title":"Chapter 12 GEOTECHNICAL SEISMIC ANALYSIS GEOTECHNICAL DESIGN MANUAL","url":"https://www.scdot.org/content/dam/scdot-legacy/business/pdf/geotech/2022-by-chapter/Chapter12-GeotechnicalSeismicAnalysis-01112022.pdf"},{"title":"Applicability of 1D site response analysis to shallow sedimentary basins: A critical evaluation through physics‐based 3D ground motion simulations - Huang - 2024 - Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics - Wiley Online Library","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/eqe.4142"},{"title":"NC92Soil: A computer code for deterministic and stochastic 1D equivalent linear seismic site response analyses | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374947177_NC92Soil_A_computer_code_for_deterministic_and_stochastic_1D_equivalent_linear_seismic_site_response_analyses"},{"title":"(PDF) An innovative computer code for 1D seismic response analysis including shear strength of soils","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/284755269_An_innovative_computer_code_for_1D_seismic_response_analysis_including_shear_strength_of_soils"},{"title":"Evaluation of One-Dimensional Seismic Site Response Analyses at Small to Large Strain Levels","url":"https://digital.lib.washington.edu/researchworks/handle/1773/37067"}]},"I've completed the web search for your query on seismic shear strain depth profiles in 1D site response analysis. The results provide comprehensive information about seismic site response analysis methods.\n\nThe search returned several relevant resources covering 1D seismic site response analysis, including discussions of:\n\n1. **Site Response Analysis Methods**: The analysis techniques can be categorized as linear (L), equivalent linear (EL), and nonlinear (NL) analyses in one dimension (1D), two dimensions (2D) and three dimensions (3D), with 1D analyses relying on the assumption that all soil layers are horizontal and infinite, and dynamic response considers vertical propagation of horizontal shear waves.\n\n2. **Shear Strain Profiles**: Studies compute lateral displacements, accelerations, shear strains, spectral accelerations, and Arias Intensities, with particular focus on understanding shear strain distributions with depth.\n\n3. **Depth Variation Effects**: In the equivalent linear (EL) analysis method, the equation of motion for the vertically propagating seismic shear waves is solved in the frequency domain.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about closed-form solutions for shear strain depth profiles, the mathematical derivations involving partial derivatives of displacement with respect to depth, or explicit formulations using gamma (γ) notation as partial derivatives. If you need more specific technical information about these mathematical relationships, you may want to search for academic papers or textbooks focused on wave propagation theory in geotechnical engineering."],"durationSeconds":6.737365834000054}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QYtdVTHpMw5mGGmdRr6pEb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"closed-form site response power-law shear modulus profile Bessel function natural frequencies mode shapes inhomogeneous stratum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A new exact approach for determining natural frequencies and mode shapes of non-uniform shear beams with arbitrary distribution of mass or stiffness - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020768399002012\"},{\"title\":\"Dispersive SH-surface waves in soil deposits of variable shear modulus - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726105800041\"},{\"title\":\"A class of inhomogeneous shear models for seismic\",\"url\":\"http://ssi.civil.ntua.gr/downloads/journals/1985-SDEE_A%20class%20of%20inhomogeneous%20shear%20models%20for%20seismic%20response%20of%20dams%20and%20embankments.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic Soil-Structure Interaction for a SDOF with Rigid Foundation Embedded in a Radially Inhomogeneous Bearing Stratum Under SH Waves | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-11898-2_81\"},{\"title\":\"Inhomogeneous beams possessing an exponential mode shape - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0093641310000479\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation\"},{\"title\":\"Closed-form dynamic stiffness formulation for exact modal analysis of tapered and functionally graded beams and their assemblies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020740321006056\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic Response of Tunnel Structures in Inhomogeneous Medium Under SH Wave: Shear Modulus in Quadratic Functional Form | Acta Mechanica Solida Sinica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10338-023-00395-y\"},{\"title\":\"Scattering of cylindrical inclusions in half space with inhomogeneous shear modulus due to SH wave | Archive of Applied Mechanics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00419-021-01975-5\"},{\"title\":\"Linear one-dimensional site response analysis in the presence of stiffness-less free surface for certain power-law heterogeneities - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726120311568\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several highly relevant sources on your topic. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Closed-Form Solutions for Inhomogeneous Strata with Power-Law Shear Modulus\n\nThe seismic response of inhomogeneous soil deposits can be explored analytically by means of one-dimensional viscoelastic wave propagation theory, with a continuously inhomogeneous stratum over a homogeneous layer of higher stiffness. A generalized parabolic function is employed to describe the variable shear wave propagation velocity in the inhomogeneous layer, and the problem is treated analytically leading to an exact solution of the Bessel type for the natural frequencies, mode shapes and base-to-surface response transfer function.\n\n## Bessel Function Solutions\n\nAnalytical methods based on Bessel functions have been applied to non-uniform structures, where differential equations are reduced to Bessel equations and other solvable equations. A Bessel equation solution exists for inhomogeneous shear models, with closed-form analytical expressions derived for natural frequencies, modal displacements, participation factors, and steady-state response functions for all values of the inhomogeneity factor.\n\n## Power-Law Heterogeneities\n\nOne-dimensional Site Response Analysis of heterogeneous soil deposits focuses on sites whose shear modulus distribution is described by means of a power law that yields zero stiffness at the free surface.\n\n## Related Applications\n\nThe shear modulus of an inhomogeneous bearing stratum assumed to vary in a power-law manner allows analytical series solutions for foundation displacement and relative displacement of superstructure to be derived using a wave function expansion method.\n\nThese sources provide comprehensive theoretical frameworks and analytical solutions relevant to your search query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"25b7a623-3bf7-4f76-ae3b-a4d2f932ad0e","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:47:47.471Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"closed-form site response power-law shear modulus profile Bessel function natural frequencies mode shapes inhomogeneous stratum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K5wV6i855q2kUJNpa2MqDv","content":[{"title":"A new exact approach for determining natural frequencies and mode shapes of non-uniform shear beams with arbitrary distribution of mass or stiffness - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020768399002012"},{"title":"Dispersive SH-surface waves in soil deposits of variable shear modulus - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726105800041"},{"title":"A class of inhomogeneous shear models for seismic","url":"http://ssi.civil.ntua.gr/downloads/journals/1985-SDEE_A%20class%20of%20inhomogeneous%20shear%20models%20for%20seismic%20response%20of%20dams%20and%20embankments.pdf"},{"title":"Dynamic Soil-Structure Interaction for a SDOF with Rigid Foundation Embedded in a Radially Inhomogeneous Bearing Stratum Under SH Waves | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-11898-2_81"},{"title":"Inhomogeneous beams possessing an exponential mode shape - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0093641310000479"},{"title":"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation","url":"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation"},{"title":"Closed-form dynamic stiffness formulation for exact modal analysis of tapered and functionally graded beams and their assemblies - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0020740321006056"},{"title":"Dynamic Response of Tunnel Structures in Inhomogeneous Medium Under SH Wave: Shear Modulus in Quadratic Functional Form | Acta Mechanica Solida Sinica | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10338-023-00395-y"},{"title":"Scattering of cylindrical inclusions in half space with inhomogeneous shear modulus due to SH wave | Archive of Applied Mechanics | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00419-021-01975-5"},{"title":"Linear one-dimensional site response analysis in the presence of stiffness-less free surface for certain power-law heterogeneities - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726120311568"}]},"Based on the search results, I found several highly relevant sources on your topic. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Closed-Form Solutions for Inhomogeneous Strata with Power-Law Shear Modulus\n\nThe seismic response of inhomogeneous soil deposits can be explored analytically by means of one-dimensional viscoelastic wave propagation theory, with a continuously inhomogeneous stratum over a homogeneous layer of higher stiffness. A generalized parabolic function is employed to describe the variable shear wave propagation velocity in the inhomogeneous layer, and the problem is treated analytically leading to an exact solution of the Bessel type for the natural frequencies, mode shapes and base-to-surface response transfer function.\n\n## Bessel Function Solutions\n\nAnalytical methods based on Bessel functions have been applied to non-uniform structures, where differential equations are reduced to Bessel equations and other solvable equations. A Bessel equation solution exists for inhomogeneous shear models, with closed-form analytical expressions derived for natural frequencies, modal displacements, participation factors, and steady-state response functions for all values of the inhomogeneity factor.\n\n## Power-Law Heterogeneities\n\nOne-dimensional Site Response Analysis of heterogeneous soil deposits focuses on sites whose shear modulus distribution is described by means of a power law that yields zero stiffness at the free surface.\n\n## Related Applications\n\nThe shear modulus of an inhomogeneous bearing stratum assumed to vary in a power-law manner allows analytical series solutions for foundation displacement and relative displacement of superstructure to be derived using a wave function expansion method.\n\nThese sources provide comprehensive theoretical frameworks and analytical solutions relevant to your search query."],"durationSeconds":7.891386041999911}}
