{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NjEj1ZH4HWHZrTXFrqn5Zm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Roesset 1977 soil amplification transfer function uniform layer viscous damping closed-form acceleration\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SOIL DAMPING FORMULATION IN NONLINEAR TIME DOMAIN SITE RESPONSE ANALYSIS | Journal of Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1142/S1363246904001420\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Soil damping formulation in nonlinear time domain site response analysis\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/279933053_Soil_damping_formulation_in_nonlinear_time_domain_site_response_analysis\"},{\"title\":\"Soil amplification: some refinements - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/026172778490041X\"},{\"title\":\"Approximate analysis of dynamic soil-structure interaction\",\"url\":\"https://escholarship.org/content/qt1cj839j2/qt1cj839j2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"1 UCRL—86217 DE82 009014 AN EVALUATION OF SOIL DAMPING TECHNIQUES USED IN SOIL\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/5070464\"},{\"title\":\"Transfer matrix approach to earthquake amplification through layered soils - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0029549375900813\"},{\"title\":\"Transfer functions for a uniform elastic soil layer underlain by rigid... | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Transfer-functions-for-a-uniform-elastic-soil-layer-underlain-by-rigid-bedrock-for_fig2_264332396\"},{\"title\":\"1 SOIL NON-LINEAR BEHAVIOR AND HYSTERETIC DAMPING IN THE SPRING-DASHPOT ANALOG\",\"url\":\"https://www.eaee.org/Media/Default/2ECCES/2ecces_eaee/1710.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic Site-Amplification Factors and Dynamic\",\"url\":\"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/WCEE2012_0336.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"1 Estimating Total System Damping for Soil- Structure Interaction Systems\",\"url\":\"https://www.pwri.go.jp/eng/ujnr/tc/a/ssi_w3/Contributions/Ostadan.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Roesset's 1977 work on soil amplification. Here's what I found:\n\nJ. M. Roesset's 1977 publication \"Soil amplification of earthquakes\" appeared in the Numerical Methods in Geotechnical Engineering book edited by C. S. Desai and J. T. Christian (McGraw-Hill, New York), pp. 649–682.\n\nThe search results show that Roesset's work is a foundational reference in the field of soil amplification analysis. The fundamentals of soil amplification have been formulated by researchers including Roesset & Whitman, and the most widely used techniques for studying one-dimensional amplification of vertically propagating seismic waves involve solution of the dynamic equations in the frequency domain with linearly viscoelastic material properties.\n\nRegarding the specific technical aspects you're asking about (transfer functions, uniform layers, viscous damping, and closed-form solutions for acceleration), the search results reference these topics in relation to soil amplification analysis, but don't provide detailed excerpts from Roesset's 1977 paper itself. The results indicate that transfer matrix approaches are used to determine amplification with various levels of damping, where the amplification term for multilayered media is found through multiplication of layer transfer matrices.\n\nTo access the specific closed-form solutions and mathematical formulations you're seeking from Roesset's 1977 work, you would need to consult the original publication directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"c13e287d-7616-4960-88d4-7ea07e3f7d2d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:47:57.465Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Roesset 1977 soil amplification transfer function uniform layer viscous damping closed-form acceleration","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01USyMNdKX9u3CwY3GJJ3cGM","content":[{"title":"SOIL DAMPING FORMULATION IN NONLINEAR TIME DOMAIN SITE RESPONSE ANALYSIS | Journal of Earthquake Engineering","url":"https://doi.org/10.1142/S1363246904001420"},{"title":"(PDF) Soil damping formulation in nonlinear time domain site response analysis","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/279933053_Soil_damping_formulation_in_nonlinear_time_domain_site_response_analysis"},{"title":"Soil amplification: some refinements - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/026172778490041X"},{"title":"Approximate analysis of dynamic soil-structure interaction","url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt1cj839j2/qt1cj839j2.pdf"},{"title":"1 UCRL—86217 DE82 009014 AN EVALUATION OF SOIL DAMPING TECHNIQUES USED IN SOIL","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/5070464"},{"title":"Transfer matrix approach to earthquake amplification through layered soils - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0029549375900813"},{"title":"Transfer functions for a uniform elastic soil layer underlain by rigid... | Download Scientific Diagram","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Transfer-functions-for-a-uniform-elastic-soil-layer-underlain-by-rigid-bedrock-for_fig2_264332396"},{"title":"1 SOIL NON-LINEAR BEHAVIOR AND HYSTERETIC DAMPING IN THE SPRING-DASHPOT ANALOG","url":"https://www.eaee.org/Media/Default/2ECCES/2ecces_eaee/1710.pdf"},{"title":"Dynamic Site-Amplification Factors and Dynamic","url":"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/WCEE2012_0336.pdf"},{"title":"1 Estimating Total System Damping for Soil- Structure Interaction Systems","url":"https://www.pwri.go.jp/eng/ujnr/tc/a/ssi_w3/Contributions/Ostadan.pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about Roesset's 1977 work on soil amplification. Here's what I found:\n\nJ. M. Roesset's 1977 publication \"Soil amplification of earthquakes\" appeared in the Numerical Methods in Geotechnical Engineering book edited by C. S. Desai and J. T. Christian (McGraw-Hill, New York), pp. 649–682.\n\nThe search results show that Roesset's work is a foundational reference in the field of soil amplification analysis. The fundamentals of soil amplification have been formulated by researchers including Roesset & Whitman, and the most widely used techniques for studying one-dimensional amplification of vertically propagating seismic waves involve solution of the dynamic equations in the frequency domain with linearly viscoelastic material properties.\n\nRegarding the specific technical aspects you're asking about (transfer functions, uniform layers, viscous damping, and closed-form solutions for acceleration), the search results reference these topics in relation to soil amplification analysis, but don't provide detailed excerpts from Roesset's 1977 paper itself. The results indicate that transfer matrix approaches are used to determine amplification with various levels of damping, where the amplification term for multilayered media is found through multiplication of layer transfer matrices.\n\nTo access the specific closed-form solutions and mathematical formulations you're seeking from Roesset's 1977 work, you would need to consult the original publication directly."],"durationSeconds":5.972557374999975}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GK6KccE3BunKSH9cgt2Wf9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gazetas 1982 inhomogeneous soil seismic response parabolic shear modulus Bessel closed-form strains\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 148, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002850\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/103879197/Seismic_shear_strains_and_seismic_coefficients_in_dams_and_embankments?f_ri=243848\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation\"},{\"title\":\"A class of inhomogeneous shear models for seismic\",\"url\":\"http://ssi.civil.ntua.gr/downloads/journals/1985-SDEE_A%20class%20of%20inhomogeneous%20shear%20models%20for%20seismic%20response%20of%20dams%20and%20embankments.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Characterisation of shear wave velocity profiles of non-uniform bi-layer soil deposits: Analytical evaluation and experimental validation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726115000718\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0267726186900011\"},{\"title\":\"Dispersive SH-surface waves in soil deposits of variable shear modulus - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726105800041\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1986SDEE....5...75D/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360208957_Seismic_Response_of_Inhomogeneous_Soil_Deposits_with_Exponentially_Varying_Stiffness\"},{\"title\":\"Nonlinear Soil - Pile - Structure Interaction in Dynamic or Seismic Response\",\"url\":\"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/WCEE2012_0037.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Gazetas' 1982 work on inhomogeneous soil seismic response. Here's what the results show:\n\nGazetas published work on \"Vibrational characteristics of soil deposits with variable wave velocity\" in the International Journal for Numerical and Analytical Methods in Geomechanics in 1982.\n\nThe search results indicate that Gazetas' 1982 work has been cited extensively in the literature on seismic response of inhomogeneous soil deposits, and it relates to analyses involving parabolic velocity models and Bessel function solutions.\n\nMore specifically, the research builds on Gazetas' foundational work: In follow-up studies, the solution to the governing equation was shown to be a Bessel equation, with values depending on the inhomogeneity parameter m for each truncation ratio.\n\nThe work involves closed-form analytical expressions for natural frequencies, modal displacements, participation factors, and steady-state response functions for all values of the inhomogeneity factor m.\n\nAdditionally, a generalized parabolic function describes the variable shear wave propagation velocity in inhomogeneous layers, with the problem treated analytically leading to an exact solution of the Bessel type for natural frequencies, mode shapes and base-to-surface response transfer function.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"85f8981d-42c3-4edb-aaa7-52cc45dbb8a9","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:47:58.488Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Gazetas 1982 inhomogeneous soil seismic response parabolic shear modulus Bessel closed-form strains","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NqZvneFF22C4Qt1q2eXQyC","content":[{"title":"Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 148, No 11","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002850"},{"title":"(PDF) Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments","url":"https://www.academia.edu/103879197/Seismic_shear_strains_and_seismic_coefficients_in_dams_and_embankments?f_ri=243848"},{"title":"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation","url":"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation"},{"title":"A class of inhomogeneous shear models for seismic","url":"http://ssi.civil.ntua.gr/downloads/journals/1985-SDEE_A%20class%20of%20inhomogeneous%20shear%20models%20for%20seismic%20response%20of%20dams%20and%20embankments.pdf"},{"title":"Characterisation of shear wave velocity profiles of non-uniform bi-layer soil deposits: Analytical evaluation and experimental validation - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726115000718"},{"title":"Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0267726186900011"},{"title":"Dispersive SH-surface waves in soil deposits of variable shear modulus - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726105800041"},{"title":"Seismic shear strains and seismic coefficients in dams and embankments - ADS","url":"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1986SDEE....5...75D/abstract"},{"title":"(PDF) Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360208957_Seismic_Response_of_Inhomogeneous_Soil_Deposits_with_Exponentially_Varying_Stiffness"},{"title":"Nonlinear Soil - Pile - Structure Interaction in Dynamic or Seismic Response","url":"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/WCEE2012_0037.pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about Gazetas' 1982 work on inhomogeneous soil seismic response. Here's what the results show:\n\nGazetas published work on \"Vibrational characteristics of soil deposits with variable wave velocity\" in the International Journal for Numerical and Analytical Methods in Geomechanics in 1982.\n\nThe search results indicate that Gazetas' 1982 work has been cited extensively in the literature on seismic response of inhomogeneous soil deposits, and it relates to analyses involving parabolic velocity models and Bessel function solutions.\n\nMore specifically, the research builds on Gazetas' foundational work: In follow-up studies, the solution to the governing equation was shown to be a Bessel equation, with values depending on the inhomogeneity parameter m for each truncation ratio.\n\nThe work involves closed-form analytical expressions for natural frequencies, modal displacements, participation factors, and steady-state response functions for all values of the inhomogeneity factor m.\n\nAdditionally, a generalized parabolic function describes the variable shear wave propagation velocity in inhomogeneous layers, with the problem treated analytically leading to an exact solution of the Bessel type for natural frequencies, mode shapes and base-to-surface response transfer function."],"durationSeconds":6.4457818749999864}}
