{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016puBbZbJSVmQD6TqtNneYi","type":"tool_result","content":"# Mathematical Derivation Content Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the full mathematical derivations you requested are not present** in this documentation page.\n\n## What Is Available\n\nThe page provides only **introductory formulas**:\n\n1. **Fundamental frequency** for uniform soil:\n   - Formula: ω₀ = πvₛ/(2H)\n   - Where vₛ = shear wave velocity, H = soil thickness\n\n2. **Characteristic site period**:\n   - Formula: Tₛ = 4H/vₛ\n\n3. **Complex impedance ratio**:\n   - Definition provided relating complex shear modulus, wave number, and shear wave velocity across layer boundaries\n\n## What Is Missing\n\nThe page does **not contain**:\n- Governing wave equation derivation for 1D SH propagation\n- Boundary conditions formulation\n- Transfer function derivation for uniform layers\n- Modal decomposition methodology\n- Natural frequencies derivation\n- Mode shapes analysis\n- Acceleration transfer function formula derivation\n- Shear strain from displacement derivation\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThe documentation explicitly references Kramer (1996) as the source for detailed derivations, stating: \"For more details, the user is encouraged to read [Kra96].\" You would need to consult that referenced textbook for the comprehensive mathematical framework you're seeking."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"ae8a1191-365f-4516-b700-3596fe389714","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:48:29.206Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":15347,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Mathematical Derivation Content Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the full mathematical derivations you requested are not present** in this documentation page.\n\n## What Is Available\n\nThe page provides only **introductory formulas**:\n\n1. **Fundamental frequency** for uniform soil:\n   - Formula: ω₀ = πvₛ/(2H)\n   - Where vₛ = shear wave velocity, H = soil thickness\n\n2. **Characteristic site period**:\n   - Formula: Tₛ = 4H/vₛ\n\n3. **Complex impedance ratio**:\n   - Definition provided relating complex shear modulus, wave number, and shear wave velocity across layer boundaries\n\n## What Is Missing\n\nThe page does **not contain**:\n- Governing wave equation derivation for 1D SH propagation\n- Boundary conditions formulation\n- Transfer function derivation for uniform layers\n- Modal decomposition methodology\n- Natural frequencies derivation\n- Mode shapes analysis\n- Acceleration transfer function formula derivation\n- Shear strain from displacement derivation\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThe documentation explicitly references Kramer (1996) as the source for detailed derivations, stating: \"For more details, the user is encouraged to read [Kra96].\" You would need to consult that referenced textbook for the comprehensive mathematical framework you're seeking.","durationMs":4719,"url":"https://nheri-simcenter.github.io/TFT-Documentation/theory.html"}}
