{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUhvzLQA6WgDAxivvwMHzY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"seismic shear strain closed-form uniform layer modal expansion gamma_n mode shape participation factor site response analytical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A uniform asymptotic expansion for the shear-wave front in a layer - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0165212594900590\"},{\"title\":\"Modal growth and non-modal growth in a stretched shear layer - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0997754603000578\"},{\"title\":\"Inelastic seismic shear amplification due to higher mode effects in reinforced concrete coupled walls - Gabriel Rivard, Steeve Ambroise, Patrick Paultre, 2022\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/87552930211053347\"},{\"title\":\"Guidelines for Estimation of Shear Wave Velocity Profiles\",\"url\":\"https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/webpeer-2012-08-bernard_r._wair_jason_t._dejong_and_thomas_shantz.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Characterisation of shear wave velocity profiles of non-uniform bi-layer soil deposits: Analytical evaluation and experimental validation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726115000718\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 3 The Seismic Wave Equation\",\"url\":\"https://igppweb.ucsd.edu/~guy/sio227a/ch3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic Velocity — GPG 0.0.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://gpg.geosci.xyz/content/physical_properties/seismic_velocity_duplicate.html\"},{\"title\":\"Shear Modulus - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/earth-and-planetary-sciences/shear-modulus\"},{\"title\":\"Analytical solution of seismic response for tunnel covered by an isolation layer under longitudinally propagating shear waves - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726124001209\"},{\"title\":\"Shear modulus - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shear_modulus\"}]\n\nThe search results provide general information about seismic wave propagation, shear modulus, and analytical methods for soil response, but they don't contain specific information about the exact technical concepts you're asking about, particularly regarding gamma_n, mode shape participation factors, and closed-form expressions for seismic shear strain using modal expansion in uniform layers.\n\nBased on the results returned, I can see that analytical methods using wave function expansion are used to solve governing equations of motion for problems involving shear, and analytical solutions have been developed for seismic responses in layered systems, including closed-form solutions using relative stiffness methods.\n\nHowever, the specific technical terminology you mentioned (gamma_n, mode shape participation factor in the context you describe) appears to be from specialized geotechnical or seismic engineering literature that isn't fully covered in these search results. To find more precise information about these specific parameters and their closed-form expressions for site response analysis, you may need to consult:\n\n1. Specialized textbooks on seismic site response analysis\n2. Journal articles in geotechnical earthquake engineering\n3. Technical papers from organizations like PEER (Pacific Earthquake Engineering Research Center) or USGS\n\nWould you like me to perform a more targeted search for any of these specific terms?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed3db8e9-bddf-493a-90e5-1f46bbf22517","uuid":"8df950dd-2aa5-4df3-8f8b-ba17f6dd51f4","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:49:21.758Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"seismic shear strain closed-form uniform layer modal expansion gamma_n mode shape participation factor site 